rr4|v|To become full; to have the whole capacity occupied; to have an abundant supply; to be satiated; as, corn fills well in a warm season; the sail fills with the wind. ; To fill a cup or glass for drinking. ; A full supply, as much as supplies want; as much as gives complete satisfaction.	o:18cp,19,3~18cp,19,3
